# ---- Harvested documents ----
# Multi-megabyte binaries mirrored from borrower sites, content-addressed by
# SHA-256. Not source: back this directory up as data, do not commit it.
data/harvest/

# ---- Research material ----
# Downloaded World Bank PDFs and real tender documents (see research/*.md).
# The notes and the gold set are tracked; the binaries are not.
research/regulations/
research/sbd/
research/samples/
research/screenshots/

# ---- Celery ----
celerybeat-schedule*
celerybeat.pid

# ---- Node / Frontend ----
node_modules/
dist/
dist-ssr/
.vite/
*.local
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*

# ---- Env / secrets ----
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ---- Docker ----
docker-compose.override.yml

# ---- Sourcing output ----
# Candidate CSVs written by the discovery scripts: names of real people,
# scraped and not yet verified. They are the reason apps/sourcing has no
# endpoint that could leak them (D21) — committing one would leak them
# permanently instead, into a history no deletion reaches.
out/

# ---- Internal working notes ----
# Team coordination and orientation notes for whoever picks the repository up
# next. Kept beside the checkout rather than in it, so a reader is never
# choosing between two overlapping accounts.
NOTES.md
TEAM.md

# ---- Editors / OS ----
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
